1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,168
My phone just exploded with ten thousand cheers for playing three chords on a dusty sidewalk.

2
00:00:06,468 --> 00:00:14,220
Every time the notification bell rings, the applause gets louder, roaring straight into my headphones.

3
00:00:14,520 --> 00:00:24,456
I look up. A businesswoman walking past me suddenly stumbles, her face instantly turning completely blank and lifeless.

4
00:00:24,756 --> 00:00:32,772
Another wave of digital cheers hits my screen. The woman slumps against the tiled wall, sobbing silently.

5
00:00:33,072 --> 00:00:40,632
I check the app. The applause counter matches the exact second her smile vanished into thin air.

6
00:00:40,932 --> 00:00:49,260
I stop strumming my guitar. The digital cheers instantly stutter, choking off into heavy, static silence.

7
00:00:49,560 --> 00:00:56,880
The weeping woman takes a deep breath, color returning to her cheeks as she looks around, confused.

8
00:00:57,180 --> 00:01:04,044
My screen flashes. A notification warns me: keep playing, or lose your audience forever.

9
00:01:04,344 --> 00:01:11,592
I stare at my guitar, then at the crowded subway platform full of living, breathing human beings.

10
00:01:11,892 --> 00:01:20,316
With trembling hands, I drop my phone onto the tracks. How loud does your applause have to be to drown out someone else's soul?
